## Core Frontend Implementation Standards

### Semantic Markup & Structure
- Use `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`, `<h1>`-`<h6>`, `<button>`, `<table>`.
- Never use `<div>` or `<span>` for clickable actions without `role="button"`, `tabindex="0"`, and keydown handlers for `Enter` and `Space`.
- All `<img>` tags must have `alt`. Informative images get concise descriptions; decorative images get `alt=""` and `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Icon buttons must have accessible names via `aria-label` or visually-hidden `.sr-only` text.

### Visual Contrast & Focus
- Text contrast must be at least **4.5:1** for regular text and **3:1** for large text (≥ 24px or ≥ 18.66px bold).
- UI component borders and active indicators must meet **3:1** contrast against adjacent backgrounds.
- Never use `outline: none` without providing an equal or better high-contrast focus indicator:
  ```css
  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #005fcc;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  ```
- Never rely on color alone to convey status or errors.

### Forms & Notifications
- Every `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` must have an associated `<label for="...">`.
- Connect error messages using `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby="[id]"` on the input.
- Announce asynchronous updates or errors with `aria-live="polite"` or `role="alert"`.

### Modal Dialogs
- Use native `<dialog>` or custom container with `role="dialog"` and `aria-modal="true"`.
- Trap keyboard focus inside while open.
- Close on `Escape` key and return focus to the trigger button.
